  <static seed="506" source="Library/UMN/calculusStewartET/s_15_1_1.pg">
    <statement><p>Use a Riemann sum to estimate the volume of the solid that lies below the surface <m>z = xy</m> and above the region <m>R = \lbrace (x,y): 0 \le x \le 3, 0 \le y \le 2\rbrace</m>.  Create the Riemann sum by subdividing <m>[0,3]</m> into <m>m = 3</m> intervals, and <m>[0,2]</m> into <m>n=2</m> intervals, and take the sample point to be the upper right corner of each rectangle.</p>
<p>Volume: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{3\cdot 2}{6}\mathopen{}\left(1+2+2+4+3+6\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
